            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="ROT01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Richard</forename>
                        <surname>Rothwell</surname>
                        <addName>Ireland</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1800-11-20">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1863-09-03"/>
                    <occupation>genre and portrait painter</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>The <title>DNB</title> has him deciding to go to Italy in 1831 but the contacts in
    the diary and his association with Mary Wollstonecraft-Shelley suggest that he does not in fact leave until the summer
    of 1832. The 1830/1 contacts, painting a portrait of Mary Shelley, do seem to support the
    identification.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
